---
// /documentation/check-it-works
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Note from '../../components/docs/Note.astro';
import Screenshot from '../../components/docs/Screenshot.astro';
---
<DocsLayout slug="check-it-works">
  <p class="docs-lede">Log in as a test user, open a record and send a message. Here's what they'll see.</p>

  <h2 id="first-time">The first time</h2>
  <p>Each user sees a short terms screen once. It explains that personal data is masked, that answers can be wrong, and that conversations are logged. They tick to say they've read your AI usage policy, then click <strong class="ui">Agree and continue</strong>.</p>
  <Screenshot id="terms-screen" />
  <p>Add a link to your company's AI usage policy in the LoomConnect AI Settings tab, under <strong>Terms and policy</strong>, and it appears on this screen.</p>

  <h2 id="every-time">Every time after</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A reminder that personal details on the record are swapped for placeholders.</li>
    <li>An agent switcher, when more than one agent works on that object.</li>
    <li><strong class="ui">Helpful</strong> and <strong class="ui">Not helpful</strong> on every answer, with an optional reason.</li>
    <li>Options to copy an answer, save it to the record as a note or task, or share the conversation.</li>
    <li>A usage view showing how much of their daily limit they've used.</li>
  </ul>
  <Screenshot id="chat-window" />

  <h2 id="ready">Ready for everyone?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The model shows Connected on the AI Agent Models tab.</li>
    <li>Everyone who'll chat has LoomConnect AI User and your provider access permission set.</li>
    <li>A usage policy is set as the default.</li>
    <li>Every object your agent reads is in the AI PII Registry.</li>
    <li>Your test user can see the agent and gets a sensible answer.</li>
  </ul>
  <Note type="check" title="That's setup done">Give the rest of the team access when you're ready. The pages below cover giving agents more to work with.</Note>
</DocsLayout>
